From 3943a37092ab976a21f34f7deba6a483e3e4f725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:22:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] feat(core): list several kinds in one call; multi-get
 and field projection (C9, C27)

Reading many things cost one call each. Job 10 of the native session
swept 33 kinds one call at a time to find what was left in a namespace
(3,599 tokens, 5 errors from guessed kinds); job 15 read 8 Deployments
in full (about 490 tokens each) to compare two fields.

resources_list:
- `kinds: [{apiVersion, kind}, ...]` lists several kinds in one call and
  returns the names per kind; a kind that fails (unknown, forbidden) is
  reported inline with its error and does not fail the call (C9);
- `all_kinds: true` lists every namespaced kind the cluster serves (by
  discovery, preferred versions, list verb), except Events, in the
  given namespace, and shows only kinds that have objects (C9);
- `fields: [paths]` returns, per object, its name and only the requested
  fields (C27).

resources_get:
- `names: [...]` reads several objects of one kind in one call, each
  object's error inline (C27);
- `fields: [paths]`, with name or names, returns only those fields.

Paths are dotted, with [N] for one list element and [*] for every
element ("spec.template.spec.containers[*].image"); a missing path gives
null. apiVersion and kind are no longer required by resources_list's
schema, nor name by resources_get's; the handlers still refuse a call
that gives neither form, with the old messages. Single-kind lists and
single gets without fields are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
